criteria:
Inclusion Criteria:

* Patients ≥ 18 years of age;
* Affected by significant carotid atherosclerosis, whether symptomatic or asymptomatic (stenosis ≥ 70% according to ECST criteria).
* Candidates for carotid ATE surgery. The criteria provided by the SICVE and ESVS guidelines will be followed for indications for surgery;
* Preoperative imaging available;

Exclusion Criteria:

* Patients who have undergone previous carotid endarterectomy (ipsilateral to the affected side);
* Patients who have undergone previous neck surgery involving cervical lymph node dissection;
* Patients who have undergone previous neck radiation therapy;
* Lack of preoperative imaging;
* Patients unable to sign informed consent.
